Z||000016||Fformula88||01-28-2001||11:44 AM||||pHoOl, to change to a T-top roof is much moreinvolved than just a sunroof.  For the sunroof, you only need to find a Fiero with one and swap the roofs.  Basically its a matter of swapping the roof panels, and is completely reversable.  As for the T-tops, your going to have to do frame work.  The roof has the frame all the way around the outside under the roof panel, so it looks like a large box.  The outside rails have to be removed and one put into the center for the roof.  I am not sure how complicated this is to do, but its definately not as easily reversed as the sunroof move.  But it would be awesome to get T-tops into the car!!<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">     <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1987 Fiero Sport Coupe *In rebuilding*<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
